{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1065636-fan-splats-fleshing-out-revenant-the-ravishing","id":1065636,"title":"Fan-splats fleshing out \"Revenant, the ravishing\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-21T02:10:28-07:00","id":1065636,"title":"Fan-splats fleshing out \"Revenant, the ravishing\"","content":"I've recently been toying with the idea of incorporating intelligent living dead into my WOD. I already read a couple of threads right here that I found interesting. Although I am aware that this subject was covered by Wraith with the Risen, I keep feeling that the living corpses need of a separate identity from ghosts. I read Zombie: the Coil, but I was looking more for something in the form of classical revenants, not much unlike &quot;western Kueijin&quot; (an Idea circulating around these forums). So finally, I'd like to ask if someone has ever seen any fan attempts to give a full template to revenants/skeletons/liches/sentient zombies types out there. ??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12201-brainstr\u00f6m","name":"Brainstr\u00f6m","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T03:35:16-07:00","id":1065652,"title":"","content":"...you know what ravish means, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T03:45:52-07:00","id":1065655,"title":"","content":"I think Strigoi- The restless is a better title.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T04:25:26-07:00","id":1065666,"title":"","content":"The Bygone Bestiary is your best bet:<br /> <br /> Alien Appearance, 1-5 pt flaw - can be used to simulate almost any appearance but zombies/skeletons/various undead are well within its scope<br /> Armor, 1-4pt special advantage - makes things harder to kill<br /> Unaging, 2 pt merit - obvious really<br /> etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T08:10:46-07:00","id":1065771,"title":"","content":"You want revenants ravishing folks? Play VtM. That is clearly what the joke is referencing, not some other fan made game. Any walking corpse can be rightly called a revenant: Kindred, Risen, those Asian vampire things I don't use, ect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T08:37:59-07:00","id":1065790,"title":"","content":"Kuei-jin do a fair amount of Ravishing without any change (when they are not running on Yin). I would suggest just making a non-Asian version of KJ, with their own Dharmas and conflicts. While it would change the setting somewhat, it would be interesting if the KJ were just living dead who created mortal mythologies to glorify their existence, and that the living dead have existed since the death of the first human (meaning that they predate the Kindred by a minimum of 500,000 years).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T12:43:33-07:00","id":1065893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1065636-fan-splats-fleshing-out-revenant-the-ravishing?p=1065790#post1065790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kuei-jin do a fair amount of Ravishing without any change (when they are not running on Yin). I would suggest just making a non-Asian version of KJ, with their own Dharmas and conflicts. While it would change the setting somewhat, it would be interesting if the KJ were just living dead who created mortal mythologies to glorify their existence, and that the living dead have existed since the death of the first human (meaning that they predate the Kindred by a minimum of 500,000 years).</div> </div> </div> </div>This what I was thinking too. Perhaps the Hungry Dead are more common and do emerge in the West from time to time. I was thinking on keeping the Quincunx almost the same with most of its influence in Mainland China and some isolated parts in the rest of the world. Hungry Dead in the West, however, might have their own Philosophies(Dharmas).I have been tossing some ideas around to give them their own identity aside from vampires, however that is tricky because the two species of undead might have to compete for the same ecological niche. Im thinking on drawing ideas and inspiration from popular stories, Geist and KotE, and so far I've come up with some rough ideas: <br /> -Perhaps some Hungry Dead just want seek the pleasure of living. This is straight foward a transcription of the Thrashing Dragons. Archetype based on the mexican Catrina or Baron Samedi<br /> -Something like the western Boneflower version. Maybe Corpus eating/dead drinking type concern with the dead but not focusing that much on ancestral worship and more on graverobbing. (Got to give them a twist though to prevent a lot of conceptual overlap with vampire necromancers) Archetype: classical grave robbing ghouls, maybe D&amp;D Liches...<br /> -A ripper type philosophy based on coming back from the dead to enact revenge or something (?) Archetype: Ghost rider, Solomon Grundy<br /> -I was also thinking about other kinds of skeletons in fiction that I can base characters on like cursed pirate skulls, or undead tomb guardians.... <br /> I was also thinking that it be an interesting thing to consider how would politics between the revenants/strigoi/Hungry Dead and let's say the local Nosferatu might be when having to share a Necropolis for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12201-brainstr\u00f6m","name":"Brainstr\u00f6m","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T06:06:06-07:00","id":1066267,"title":"","content":"I had Revenant the Abyss as my Splat name. Did some conversion and added a backstory from the tv show Brimstone. A player ame up with his own dharma equivalent : Path of the Demon Knight. Also added a western equivalent of Yomi so the cosmology is different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T11:32:25-07:00","id":1066487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hachiman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1065636-fan-splats-fleshing-out-revenant-the-ravishing?p=1066267#post1066267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had Revenant the Abyss as my Splat name. Did some conversion and added a backstory from the tv show Brimstone. A player ame up with his own dharma equivalent : Path of the Demon Knight. Also added a western equivalent of Yomi so the cosmology is different.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds awesome. Specially the Demon Knight Dharma. The only problem is that I m already using the term Abyss for something else... I've never seen the show but I like the concept of these revenants believing they were brought back to serve as vigilantes on the name of heavenly justice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12201-brainstr\u00f6m","name":"Brainstr\u00f6m","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T16:13:37-07:00","id":1066616,"title":"","content":"Well, the Western version of Yomi is Hell, of which there are thousands of different version within the Western world (some within the same religion).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}